Revision history for agent-construction-kit

{{$NEXT}}
    - Add claude-with, the launcher behind every starter: it loads a provider
      definition, finds the key, sets the environment and starts Claude Code.
      Definitions ship for MiniMax, Moonshot AI Kimi, Ollama Cloud, Fireworks
      AI and OpenAI through claude-code-proxy.
    - Add ack-wrappers, which creates, tests and removes the starters
      (claude_with_<name>), opens the key file in an editor, changes provider
      values and adds starters for local model servers.
    - Add ack-proxy, which reports on the claude-code-proxy behind the openai
      provider, lists its models, checks the model slots and sets up a user
      service on Linux.
    - Add ack-doctor, a read-only check of the machine: Claude Code, git, the
      plugins agent teams build on, optional tools and the installed starters.
    - Add the agent-construction-kit skill, which sets up a machine in plain
      questions: prerequisites, a starter per provider, OpenAI through the
      proxy, and local models.
    - Find claude-code-proxy in ~/.local/bin and ~/bin when it is not on PATH
      (or at ACK_PROXY_BIN); ack-proxy status and ack-doctor say so, and the
      sign-in hints then carry the full path.
    - ack-proxy check-slots checks the small-model slot too.
    - ack-wrappers new-local tells you to pass --replace when the definition
      is its own; ack-wrappers --help prints the whole header.
    - ack-wrappers install reports "path pending" instead of "path missing"
      once path-fix has added the directory to the shell profile.